---
import { BaseLayout } from "@walle/layouts";
import { SectionHeaderStandard } from "@walle/components";

const lastUpdated = "January 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  headerTitle="Privacy Policy"
  headerDescription="How this template project handles personal data."
  headerRobots="noindex, follow"
>
  <SectionHeaderStandard
    title="Privacy Policy"
    subtitle="Sample text. Replace it with your own policy before going live."
    variant="secondary"
  />

  <article class="legal">
    <p class="legal__meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="legal__notice">
      <strong>Template notice.</strong> This is placeholder copy shipped with the Walle scaffold. It is
      not legal advice. Replace every section with a policy reviewed for your jurisdiction before publishing.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Overview</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains what information the website collects, why it is collected, and
      how it is used. By using the site you agree to the practices described here.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Usage data</strong>: anonymous analytics such as pages viewed and referrer.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Provided data</strong>: anything you submit through a form or contact channel.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Technical data</strong>: browser type, device, and IP address, used to serve the
        site.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
    <p>
      Data is used to operate and improve the site, respond to requests, and keep the service
      secure. It is never sold. Aggregated, anonymized statistics may be used to understand traffic.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      The site may store cookies for essential functionality and, where enabled, analytics. You can
      block cookies in your browser; essential features will still work.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Some pages rely on third-party providers (for example, hosting or analytics). Those providers
      process data under their own privacy terms.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, or delete your data,
      or to object to its processing. Contact us to exercise any of these rights.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy can be sent to the address listed on the site. Update this section
      with your real contact details.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-3xl) var(--space-xl) var(--space-4xl);
  }

  .legal__meta {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .legal__notice {
    background: var(--surface-alt);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--secondary);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0;
    padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .legal ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .legal li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }
</style>
